{"title":"G4.7 Targeted Implementation Readiness + Compressed P31 Design v0.1"}
</properties>
<iconMetadata>{"type":"emoji","emoji":"🧱"}</iconMetadata>
<content>
<callout icon="✅" color="green_bg">
	**P30 targeted readiness verdict: READY_FOR_P31_WITH_EMBEDDED_I0.** G4.7 can start from the exact post-G4.6 branch boundary. One pre-G5 primitive gap is confirmed: ImageContent rendering is still a checkerboard placeholder. The gap is not ignored and will not force a separate control round-trip; the G4.7 P31 package includes a narrow I0 image/resource closure before final success.
</callout>
# 1. Execution Anchor
- repository: `Mostorm-Labs/axiom`
- execution branch: `codex/g4-7-development`
- exact pre-G4.7 revision: `68b925e53b092657f3415c3d3992a451a8515598`
- anchor relation: ancestor
- G4.6-C automation/evidence result in ancestry: `5194d5ccf186e49a45311b39a831d1c9460e043e`
- combined physical execution-order amendment: <mention-page url="https://app.notion.com/p/3f34c57a590c8169af22eabaaef2bf4f"/>
# 2. Repository Reality
Confirmed:
- canonical RichText V1 schema already exists;
- RuntimeScene and DirectReferenceSource carry RichText semantic/reference records;
- current BoundsSystem uses a heuristic RichText width/height estimate;
- headless/reference RichText drawing is still rectangle-placeholder geometry rather than production shaping/layout;
- locked `r1-full-skia-sdk.lock.json` provides richtext + HarfBuzz + ICU capabilities;
- POC-04 already proves SkParagraph + SkUnicode ICU with explicit bundled font bytes;
- `deps.lock.json` pins Roboto Regular and Noto Sans CJK subset hashes;
- current ImageReferenceCommand uses a deterministic checkerboard placeholder, so a replayable production image decode/materialization workload is not yet closed.
# 3. Frozen Implementation Stack
Production Text Runtime must consume the locked R1 Full Skia SDK:
- SkParagraph
- SkShaper
- SkUnicode ICU
- bundled HarfBuzz / ICU from the locked SDK
Stable Text Runtime / Scene contracts remain renderer-neutral. No Skia/native font handles may escape into stable public or Scene contracts.
POC-04 is reference/evidence input, not production ownership. G4.7 may reuse validated ideas/fixtures but must materialize production modules under current runtime ownership.
# 4. Compressed Execution Topology
Single repo-local task package: `GT-G4.7`
Internal slices execute continuously under one frozen closure contract:
```plain text
G47-I0  Pre-G5 Image/Resource Primitive Closure
  ↓
G47-A   Production Text Runtime + Font/Profile
  ↓
G47-B   Scene / Bounds / Resource Invalidation
  ↓
G47-C   Direct Reference + Production Render + Edit Locality
  ↓
G47-D   Text Performance Playground + Automated Qualification Bundle
  ↓
READY_FOR_COMBINED_G4_PHYSICAL_QUALIFICATION
```
No separate P31 is required between these internal slices unless an explicit frozen blocker is reached.
# 5. G47-I0 — Image/Resource Primitive Closure
Purpose: close the existing pre-G5 placeholder gap without changing Image semantics.
Required:
- explicit runtime image-resource provider/resolver seam keyed by canonical ResourceId;
- real encoded image bytes → SkCodec/decode → renderable image materialization path;
- missing/ready generation observation;
- deterministic bundled test image resource;
- replayable cold/warm decode/materialization workload;
- ImageContent source-rect/content-mode behavior covered;
- resource-only availability change causes zero canonical operation.
Forbidden:
- no new Image canonical fields;
- no network fetch ownership in Render Core;
- no G5 resource-budget/cache policy;
- no Product Shell resource state.
# 6. G47-A — Text Runtime + Font/Profile
Required:
- renderer-neutral `RichTextLayoutService` or repository-equivalent;
- explicit `LayoutContext/Constraint`;
- paragraph/run/style consumption;
- derived lines/fragments/shaped runs/local bounds;
- future editing geometry mapping seam;
- FontResource provider/resolver;
- exact face resolution;
- deterministic font generation tracking;
- pinned Roboto + Noto Sans CJK test/qualification resources;
- no OS/browser fallback;
- no nearest-weight / synthetic bold / synthetic italic.
# 7. G47-B — Scene / Bounds / Resource Invalidation
Required:
- replace heuristic RichText bounds with derived production layout bounds;
- RichText layout contribution enters Scene/Bounds/Spatial through accepted derived-state ownership;
- EditRichText invalidates only affected text layout/bounds;
- SetTransforms reuses local layout;
- camera/zoom causes no local relayout;
- Font Missing→Ready causes derived invalidation with zero Operation/SemanticGeneration mutation;
- preserve old/new visual contribution for downstream G5 damage.
# 8. G47-C — Render + Locality
Required:
- same TextLayoutSnapshot consumed by Direct/NonTiled correctness path and production Skia path;
- current rectangle placeholder is no longer production RichText rendering;
- transform/camera negative controls;
- EditRichText insert/delete/split/merge/inline-style/paragraph-style locality;
- no SemanticDocument read from normal Render Core frame path.
# 9. G47-D — Performance / Automated Qualification
Required workload families:
- text-many-small
- text-long
- text-style-mixed
- text-edit-local
- text-font-cold-warm
- text-transform
- text-camera
- structured-grid-proxy
- image-resource-cold-warm
Required automated corpus:
- Latin
- punctuation/numbers
- CJK
- mixed Latin+CJK
- combining marks
- exact-glyph emoji where bundled resources contain the glyph
Full product RTL/bidi schema remains deferred.
Required output:
- Text Performance Playground;
- deterministic layout/reference digests;
- font/resource corpus identities;
- workload replay;
- `~100K` mixed Shape+RichText structured-grid proxy;
- Windows/Web/Android build/automated qualification;
- screenshot/trace hooks for later physical qualification.
# 10. Physical Boundary
G4.7 P32 does not wait for real-device visual observation.
P32 terminal success is:
`READY_FOR_COMBINED_G4_PHYSICAL_QUALIFICATION`
The later combined physical phase must consume:
- deferred G4.6 physical obligations;
- G4.7 small/large text;
- weights/styles;
- 25/100/400% zoom;
- DPR/resize;
- dense text/grid proxy;
- missing→ready resource transition;
- exact-face / fallback drift;
- Direct/NonTiled vs production visual parity;
- Windows/Web/Android profiles.
No G4.6/G4.7 Gate PASS and no G5 entry is claimed before that combined physical phase closes.
# 11. Hard Non-goals
Still deferred:
- TextEditSession
- caret/text selection interaction
- IME composition
- EditorProjection
- native/DOM editor overlays
- Clipboard
- ExternalSurface
- Table semantics
- new RichText canonical width/height/TextBox fields
- full bidi schema
- G5 Tile/RenderGroup/RasterCache/Scheduler/ResourceBudget implementation
</content>
</page>

